# Environment for Claude DESKTOP's local GitHub MCP server, resolved by
# `op run --env-file` at launch. Linked to ~/.config/gh/mcp.env.
#
# SAFE TO COMMIT: every value here is an `op://` SECRET REFERENCE, never a
# secret. `op run` resolves it in-process and injects the result into the
# child's environment; the resolved token never touches this file, the config
# that names it, argv (so it cannot leak via `ps`), or a transcript.
#
# This replaced the `gh-mcp-stdio` wrapper script on 2026-08-20. The wrapper
# existed only to read the PAT and export it, which is precisely what `op run`
# does natively — see dot-claude/DECISIONS.md.
#
# The ref is QUOTED nowhere here because dotenv does not word-split, but the
# title is space-free `kebab-case` regardless: every other consumer re-parses
# `op://` refs through `sh -c`, where a space silently breaks resolution. That
# invariant is account-wide (CLAUDE.md, "Vault item titles are kept space-free").
#
# ONE credential, ONE source of truth: this same `claude-git-pat` item also
# backs agent git auth (`op-agent git-credential`) and Claude Code's GitHub MCP
# (`op-agent header`). Rotating the vault item rotates all three at once, which
# is exactly why the value is not duplicated into a 1Password Environment.
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=op://claude-agent/claude-git-pat/credential
